//- TRANSITIONS: Lemon's dissolve is the default, so a slide that moves differently says something. Each of reveal's own transitions is shown where its move means something. Lemon's rules step aside for any slide with a data-transition (motion/_transitions.scss).

section(data-spine="Transitions")
  section.divider
    h2 Transitions
    p One dissolve by default, and reveal's own when the move means something.
    p data-transition on a section; motion/_transitions.scss

  section.statement(data-spine-section="Dissolve")
    h2 Every slide dissolves.
    p Nothing flies by default, so when something does, it means something.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li transition: "lemon" in js/reveal-config.js. Moving down a stack dissolves faster than moving to the next idea.

  section.statement(data-spine-section="None")
    h2 Everything is fine.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li The setup, on the normal dissolve.

  section.statement.is-shout(data-transition="none")
    h2 It is not fine.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="none": a smash cut. The punchline lands the instant you press the key.

  section.statement(data-spine-section="Fade")
    h2 I'll just fix one small bug.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li The setup.

  section.statement.lead-in(data-transition="fade" data-transition-speed="slow")
    p Four hours later.
    h2 I have rewritten the build.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="fade" with data-transition-speed="slow": a long crossfade says time passed.

  section.statement.lead-in(data-transition="slide" data-spine-section="Slide")
    p Step one.
    h2 Write the markup.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="slide" on every step: the steps of one sequence push each other along, so the room feels the order.

  section.statement.lead-in(data-transition="slide")
    p Step two.
    h2 Style it.

  section.statement.lead-in(data-transition="slide")
    p Step three.
    h2 Script it, if you must.

  section.statement.lead-in(data-transition="convex" data-spine-section="Convex")
    p What the designer sees:
    h2 A button.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="convex" turns the deck like a cube: the same thing, seen from another side.

  section.statement.lead-in(data-transition="convex")
    p What the developer sees:
    h2 Eleven states and a spinner.

  section.statement(data-transition="concave" data-spine-section="Concave")
    h2 It just works.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="concave" folds inward: from the surface of a thing into how it works.

  section(data-transition="concave")
    h3 Under the hood
    pre(data-file="it-just-works.js")
      code.js(data-trim).
        try {
          itJustWorks();
        } catch {
          // it does not just work
          location.reload();
        }

  section(data-spine-section="Zoom")
    h3 The sign-up form
    ul
      li Name
      li Email
      li Password
      li Confirm password
      li Sign up
    aside.notes
      ul
        li The whole thing first, on the normal dissolve.

  section.statement(data-transition="zoom")
    h2 Confirm password.
    p.aside (why is this still here)
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="zoom": dive into one detail of what came before.

  section.statement(data-transition="zoom-in fade-out" data-spine-section="Mixed")
    h2 Arrive loud, leave quiet.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition="zoom-in fade-out": the first word is how the slide arrives, the second how it leaves. Any pair works, e.g. "slide-in fade-out".

  section.statement(data-transition="slide" data-transition-speed="fast")
    h2 A quick aside.
    p.aside (data-transition-speed="fast")
    aside.notes
      ul
        li data-transition-speed="fast" or "slow" changes the pace of any transition.

  section.over-media(data-background-image="img/gif/simone_lemon_maker_faire.gif" data-background-size="cover" data-spine-section="Backgrounds")
    h2 The words dissolve.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li Two over-media slides in a row: the words dissolve as usual...

  section.over-media(data-background-image="img/gif/shooty-frooty.gif" data-background-size="cover" data-background-transition="zoom")
    h2 The picture zooms.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li ...while data-background-transition="zoom" moves the picture separately. Reveal's default for backgrounds is a fade (backgroundTransition in the config).
